"3241","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3241 Arabic Hadees: 2214"
"3242","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3242 Arabic Hadees: 814"
"3243","On the authority of Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani: He went to the Mosque of Damascus early in the morning, and he met Shaddad ibn Aws and al-Sunabihi with him. I said: ""Where are you two intending, may Allah have mercy on you?"" They said: ""We intend to visit a sick brother of ours."" So I went with them until we entered upon that man. They said to him: ""How did you wake up?"" He said: ""I woke up by the blessing and favor of Allah."" Shaddad said: ""Receive glad tidings, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Allah the Exalted says: ""When I afflict a believing servant of Mine with a trial, and he praises Me and shows patience over what I have afflicted him with, he will rise from that bed of his as pure from sins as the day his mother gave birth to him. And the Lord says to the recording angels: 'I have confined My servant and afflicted him, so record for him the reward that you used to record for him before that, while he was healthy.'""'"""""
"3244","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3244 Arabic Hadees: 496"
"3245","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3245 Arabic Hadees: 3598"
"3246","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3246 Arabic Hadees: 1233"
"3247","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3247 Arabic Hadees: 875"
"3248","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3248 Arabic Hadees: 88"
"3249","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3249 Arabic Hadees: 306"
"3250","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3250 Arabic Hadees: 3614"
"3251","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3251 Arabic Hadees: 690"
"3252","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3252 Arabic Hadees: 3225"
"3253","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3253 Arabic Hadees: 327"
"3254","Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi narrated from a man of his people who said: I sought the Prophet ﷺ but could not find him, so I sat down. Then I saw a group of people among whom he was, but I did not recognize him. He was reconciling between them. When he finished, some of them stood up with him and said: ""O Messenger of Allah!"" When I saw that, I said: ""Upon you be peace, O Messenger of Allah! Upon you be peace, O Messenger of Allah! Upon you be peace, O Messenger of Allah!"" He said: ""Indeed, 'Upon you be peace' is the greeting of the dead. Indeed, 'Upon you be peace' is the greeting of the dead"" (three times). ""When a man meets his Muslim brother, let him say: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.'"" Then the Prophet ﷺ replied to me: ""And upon you and the mercy of Allah, and upon you and the mercy of Allah, and upon you and the mercy of Allah."""""
"3255","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3255 Arabic Hadees: 1423"
"3256","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3256 Arabic Hadees: 3612"
"3257","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3257 Arabic Hadees: 824"
"3258","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when death approaches the believer and he witnesses what he witnesses, he would wish for his soul to depart, and Allah loves to meet him. And the believer's soul is taken up to the heaven, and the souls of the believers come to him, asking him about their acquaintances among the people of the earth. If he says: 'I left so-and-so in the world,' they are pleased with that. And if he says: 'So-and-so has died,' they say: 'He was not brought to us.' And the believer is made to sit up in his grave and is asked: 'Who is your Lord?' He says: 'My Lord is Allah.' It is said: 'Who is your Prophet?' He says: 'My Prophet is Muhammad (peace be upon him).' It is said: 'What is your religion?' He says: 'My religion is Islam.' Then a door is opened for him in his grave, and it is said (or he is told): 'Look at your place.' Then he sees the grave, as if it were but a nap.And when death approaches the enemy of Allah and he witnesses what he witnesses, he does not wish for his soul to depart ever, and Allah hates to meet him. Then when he sits in his grave or is made to sit, it is said to him: 'Who is your Lord?' He says: 'I do not know!' It is said: 'May you never know!' Then a door from Hell is opened for him, and he is struck a blow that is heard by every creature except the two weighty ones (jinn and men). Then it is said to him: 'Sleep as the mangled one sleeps.' I said to Abu Hurayrah: 'What is the mangled one (al-manhush)?' He said: 'The one whom beasts and vermin eat away.' Then his grave constricts upon him."""""
"3259","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3259 Arabic Hadees: 1609"
"3260","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3260 Arabic Hadees: 3614"
"3261","On the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Mulaykah, he said: I was with ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar while we were waiting for the funeral of Umm Abān bint ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, and with him was ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān. Then Ibn ʿAbbās came, led by his guide. It seemed he informed him of Ibn ʿUmar's place, so he came and sat beside me, and I was between them. Then there was a sound from the house. Ibn ʿUmar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: ""Indeed the deceased is punished by the weeping of his family over him."" ʿAbdullāh narrated it as a general statement (mursalah).Ibn ʿAbbās said: We were with the Commander of the Faithful ʿUmar until, when we were at Al-Bayḍāʾ, he saw a man sitting in the shade of a tree. He said to me: ""Go and find out who that is."" So I went and found it was Ṣuhayb. I returned to him and said: ""You commanded me to find out for you who that is, and it is Ṣuhayb."" He said: ""Tell him to catch up with us."" I said: ""He has his family with him."" He said: ""Even if his family is with him."" And perhaps Ayyūb said: ""Once, to catch up with us."" When we reached Medina, the Commander of the Faithful did not stay long before he was struck (assassinated). Ṣuhayb came and said: ""O my brother! O my companion!"" ʿUmar said: ""Did you not know, or did you not hear that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed the deceased is punished by some of the weeping of his family over him'?"" As for ʿAbdullāh, he narrated it as a general statement, and as for ʿUmar, he said: ""By some of the weeping...""So I came to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and mentioned ʿUmar's statement to her. She said: ""No, by Allah! The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not say that the deceased is punished by the weeping of anyone! But the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed the disbeliever is increased by Allah, Mighty and Majestic, in punishment by the weeping of his family over him.' (She said:) And Allah is He who causes laughter and weeping. (And no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another) (Fāṭir: 18).""Ayyūb said: And Ibn Abī Mulaykah said: Al-Qāsim narrated to me: When the statement of ʿUmar and Ibn ʿUmar reached ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: ""You are narrating to me from two men who are neither liars nor accused of lying, but hearing can err."""""
"3262","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3262 Arabic Hadees: 1131"
"3263","Zayd ibn Thabit said: While the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) was in a garden belonging to Banu al-Najjar, riding a mule of his, and we were with him, it shied and nearly threw him. There he found six, five, or four graves—Al-Jurayri was uncertain. He said: ""Who knows the occupants of these graves?"" A man said: ""I do."" He said: ""When did these people die?"" He said: ""They died in polytheism."" He said: ""Indeed, this nation will be tried in their graves. Were it not that you would cease burying one another, I would have asked Allah to let you hear the punishment of the grave that I hear."" Zayd said: Then he turned his face towards us and said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the Fire."" They said: ""We seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the Fire."" He said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave."" They said: ""We seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave."" He said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from trials, both the apparent and the hidden."" They said: ""We seek refuge with Allah from trials, both the apparent and the hidden."" He said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from the trial of the Dajjal."" They said: ""We seek refuge with Allah from the trial of the Dajjal."""""
